								<span id="lblHtml"><font color="Black" size="2"><P><STRONG>Guild Charter</STRONG></P>
<P>We are the Coven of Defiance of Vazaelle, a casual organized network of<BR>friends who believe that a sense of community is paramount to the Everquest<BR>experience.&nbsp; We make an effort to present ourselves to Norrath and outlaying<BR>zones as keepers of honor and good faith.&nbsp; We will help when we can,<BR>unselfishly, while sharing knowledge and mastery when it will benefit<BR>others.&nbsp; We uphold a high standard of conduct and will always discourage any<BR>activities that reflect poorly upon our membership whose beliefs we defend.<BR>Stand against us and ye shall feel our wrath.</P>
<P><BR><STRONG>Philosophy</STRONG></P>
<P>We are currently a small organization of around 30-50 members.&nbsp; Many of our<BR>members are casual gamers and do not spend hours every day on line.&nbsp; Growth<BR>beyond our ability to interact well with each other will never be forced but<BR>a natural progression based on the members themselves.&nbsp; Coven of Defiance<BR>does not hold mandatory events.&nbsp; You may participate on as casual basis as<BR>you like.&nbsp; However, keep in mind that the success of any organized event<BR>depends highly on attendance and representation of all classes.&nbsp; The focus<BR>of guild events is not to push the guild to have the best gear, or to gain<BR>bragging rights; moreover events focus primarily on having fun, being<BR>organized, and accomplishing through unity.&nbsp; You are encouraged to level at<BR>your own pace.&nbsp; Racing for levels can sometimes mean missing some of the<BR>finer things.&nbsp; This does not mean that the guild will not help you level.</P>
<P>We are not a “career” guild, although focusing on leveling and epic quests<BR>is not discouraged.&nbsp; We feel it is important not to lose touch with the<BR>truly important things in life such as your real life family, academics,<BR>your job, and your health to name a few.&nbsp; Spending 18 hours a day on line is<BR>neither productive nor healthy.&nbsp; You may make of the guild anything you wish<BR>but do not be selfish.&nbsp; Do not expect the guild to make sure you have fun or<BR>drop what they are doing to help you complete a quest.&nbsp; How you play is up<BR>to you.&nbsp; Through CoD and our allies, anything is possible for those who are<BR>willing to work for their goals and show compassion for others in the<BR>process.&nbsp; Establishing close ties with friends outside the guild is also<BR>encouraged; one can never have too many friends.&nbsp; We strive to always<BR>support the desires of others and to help make their goals attainable.</P>
<P><BR><STRONG>Guild Chat</STRONG></P>
<P>Use of the chat channel should be for conversation, planning groups, staying<BR>in touch and guild events.&nbsp; Please do not use guild chat to spam auctions,<BR>do price checks, or beg for equipment or money.&nbsp; Profanity should not be<BR>used in any public forum.&nbsp; Also, personal issues between members will not be<BR>broadcast in our public forum.&nbsp; Conduct deemed as damaging that is broadcast<BR>over guild chat will result in removal without warning.</P>
<P>If you need a resurrection or a port, do not repeat your request over and<BR>over.&nbsp; Chances are that if no one answers up, then they are not able to help<BR>you.&nbsp; Clerics and porting classes should not be expected to leave their<BR>groups to help you recover or at your convenience.&nbsp;&nbsp; Do not expect that<BR>people are watching guild chat all the time.&nbsp; Silence does not necessarily<BR>mean that people are ignoring you.</P></font></span>
							
